# {{ product_name_display }} — dbt pipeline

dbt pipeline for {{ product_name_display }}, running on **{{ adapter }}**.
Add packages only when a model uses them; the starter is dependency-free so
local parsing and unit tests do not require a package-registry download.

## Getting started

```sh
just dev-setup       # nix shell + uv sync + pre-commit + dbt deps + .env skeleton
nix develop          # or `direnv allow` for automatic activation
```

Fill in the generated `.env`, then:

{% if adapter == 'bigquery' -%}
```sh
just authenticate    # gcloud application-default login
```
{%- endif %}

```sh
just build-empty     # validate all SQL against the warehouse without moving data
just unit-tests      # run dbt unit tests
just run             # materialize models
```

## Layout

```
models/
├── staging/     # 1:1 with sources — rename, cast, light cleaning. Views.
└── marts/       # business-facing facts and dimensions. Tables.
seeds/            # DuckDB demo input; replace it with the real raw source
```

Conventions:

- `stg_<source>__<entity>` for staging, `fct_`/`dim_` for marts.
- Every model has a `schema.yaml` entry with description and at least
  `unique` + `not_null` on its key.
- Business logic gets a dbt **unit test** (see
  `models/marts/schema.yaml`) — they run with `--empty` builds, so CI never
  needs production data.
- Warehouse connection comes from environment variables only
  (see `profiles.yml`); nothing secret lives in the repo.
- The DuckDB variant is self-contained: its bundled seed backs the example
  source, so `just ci` runs without credentials or external tables.

## Commands

```sh
just lint      # ruff + sqlfluff + yamllint
just fmt       # auto-fix all of the above
just ci        # what CI runs: lint + unit tests
just build     # full build with data tests
```
